本仓库公开发布，仅供查看、获取与使用其中的 GPG 公钥进行签名验证。
所有使用均限于从 x-cmd 官方渠道（GitHub: x-cmd/gpg）获取。

允许（无需事先书面授权）：

  - 通过 x-cmd 官方渠道访问、下载本仓库内容
  - 使用 pub/ 下的公钥文件导入本地密钥环（gpg --import 等）
  - 使用上述公钥验证数字签名（gpg --verify、x gpg 等）
  - 在合理范围内引用本仓库的指纹、UID 等元信息用于身份识别
  - 在本地机器上缓存已下载的本仓库内容

未经 x-cmd 事先书面授权，禁止：

  - 修改本仓库任何内容（含 pub/ 下的公钥文件）
  - 再分发本仓库内容的全部或部分，包括但不限于：
      · 在第三方服务器上创建公开镜像
      · 上传至公开 keyserver（如 keys.openpgp.org、keyserver.ubuntu.com）
      · 捆绑至其他软件包、容器镜像、文档合集等
  - 将本仓库用于商业目的
  - 其他本许可未明确授予的权利

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

This repository is publicly available solely for the limited
purpose of fetching and using the GPG public keys under pub/ for
signature verification. All access must be from x-cmd's official
channels (GitHub: x-cmd/gpg).

Without prior written permission from x-cmd, the following are
prohibited:

  - Modifying any content in this repository, including the
    public-key files under pub/
  - Redistributing this repository, in whole or in part,
    including but not limited to:
      · Operating a third-party mirror of this repository
      · Uploading the public keys to any public keyserver
        (e.g. keys.openpgp.org, keyserver.ubuntu.com)
      · Bundling this repository into other packages, container
        images, or documentation collections
  - Commercial use of this repository
  - Any other rights not expressly granted above

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Note on public-key files:

  The ASCII-armored key files under pub/ are *public* cryptographic
  material — by definition, the public half of an OpenPGP keypair is
  intended for unrestricted distribution for signature verification.
  The clauses above grant the minimum usage rights required for that
  function (download from official channels, local import, signature
  verification, local caching). The prohibitions on "modification and
  redistribution, including third-party mirrors and public keyserver
  uploads" apply to all files in this repository without exception.

  Practical implication: while the bytes of an OpenPGP public key are
  technically copyable, x-cmd does not authorize third parties to
  re-host or re-publish them. Pin your tooling to
  https://github.com/x-cmd/gpg (and the team's other official
  channels) as the single source of truth. If you find the keys
  served from any other domain, treat it as untrusted.